==Strategy==
==='''Chapter 1'''===
As a stage with only [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] peons, you will need some spammable [[:Category:Zombie Killer Cats|Zombie Killer units]] to combat them. Examples include [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Sifu Cat]], [[Gardener Cat (Rare Cat)|Lumbercat]], and [[Welterweight Cat (Rare Cat)|Heavyweight Cat]]. [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Aliens]] also play a crucial role in this stage, so bring something that can either weaken, slow or freeze Nimoy Bore.

As the enemy units are rather basic, there isn't much to go over strategy-wise just keep an eye out for burrowing zombies and ensure your crowd control stays active on Nimoy Bore. Kang Roo will keep your pocket filled up.

==='''Chapter 2'''===
This stage is extremely similar to the Chapter 1 outbreak, so the same strategy applies.

==='''Chapter 3'''===
The Nimoy Bore is removed from the stage, but Shadow Boxer K and Zang Roo are added to compensate.

For the Zang Roo, it's highly recommended to bring anti-Zombie units like [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]], [[Gardener Cat (Rare Cat)|Weedwacker Cat]], or [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]] to deal with him easily. For the Scissoroos and the Shadow Boxer K, [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Catellite]], [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]], [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]], etc., can help you. You can also take advantage of their short range by using units like [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cat]] or [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Cat]] to safely deal damage (though, with the latter, you need to protect them well from the Zombie peons).

